Tue Nov 10 22:04:13 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- Update to upstream release 1.4.0
- Upstream 1.4.0 requires zig 0.17.0; Tumbleweed now ships zig0.17
  (zig-rpm-macros0.17), which Provides zig = 0.17.0. Bump %global
  zig_ver and the BuildRequires floor to 0.17.0, and ZIG_VER in
  update.sh accordingly (the auto-HOLD guard no longer trips).
- Add BuildRequires: pkgconfig(egl) (Mesa-libEGL-devel): the zig build
  links -legl via glad_egl.c (226/229 steps passed without it; the
  missing egl soname was the only failure).
- zig 0.17 honors DESTDIR for --prefix but NOT for an absolute
  --prefix-lib-dir; the lib install stepped to /usr/lib64 directly and the
  build failed AccessDenied on the OBS workers. Pass a relative
  --prefix-lib-dir (lib64) so libraries land under %{buildroot}.
- 1.4.0's zig install places libghostty-vt.{a,pc}, libghostty-vt-static.pc
  and the unversioned .so trio at %{_libdir} top level (not only under
  %{_libdir}/pkgconfig); remove all of them, as the package ships the
  application only. Fixes the unpackaged-files check failure.
- Fix vendor.tar.zst layout for zig 0.17: the deps CDN re-exported its
  tarballs, so `zig fetch` output must be extracted into
  vendor/zig/p/<manifest-hash>/ with package contents at the root
  (strip-components=1, then flatten single-wrapper dirs), not left as
  raw .tar.gz blobs; zig --system rejects the previous layout
  ("package not found at .../p/<hash>"). update.sh's
  fetch_vendor_cache now does the extract+flatten itself.

