Thu Oct 22 05:11:02 UTC 2026 - Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>

- version 1.3.1-0
- Build with -Dstrip=true instead of the previously forced -Dstrip=false
  (spec + debian.rules): upstream's own default for ReleaseFast IS strip
  (src/build/Config.zig: "Default true for fast and small releases"), and
  the forced false shipped /usr/bin/ghostty with its full .symtab. OBS's
  brp-15-strip-debug only runs `strip --strip-debug`, which is a no-op on
  a binary that has no .debug sections (verified: size unchanged, file(1)
  still "not stripped"), so rpmlint reported W: unstripped-binary-or-object.
  ReleaseFast emits no DWARF at all (readelf -S: .symtab only), so there
  is no debug info to lose and no -debuginfo package is produced either
  way. Manual strip is NOT used (openSUSE:Packaging_checks) - this only
  changes the upstream build option to upstream's documented default.

